# Dedicated ignore-file for ops/docker/Dockerfile.backend.
#
# BuildKit prefers "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" over the repo-root ".dockerignore".
# So this file FULLY REPLACES the root .dockerignore for the backend build — the root one
# (which strips packages/backend for the M1 st-bundle image) is intentionally NOT consulted
# here, leaving the M1 build untouched. Patterns below are relative to the build context root.

# Host-installed deps / build caches — always re-installed inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo

# VCS / editor / logs / secrets.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The backend image only needs packages/backend and its single workspace dep @miniapp/shared.
packages/frontend
legacy

# Everything else is irrelevant to installing + running the backend.
vendor
docs
ops
scripts
platform-assets
Database
*.md
tmp-*
